    "approach": "The problem requires printing the squares of numbers from 1 to 5 for each test case. This can be achieved by using a simple loop to iterate over the numbers 1 to 5 and calculating their squares using the multiplication operator.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T * 5), O(T) per test case. No precomputation is required.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) — the space used does not grow with the size of the input.",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int T;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &T) != 1) return 0;\n    for (int tc = 0; tc < T; ++tc) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 5; ++i) {\n            printf(\"%d - %d\\n\", i, i * i);\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "C++": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(NULL);\n    int T;\n    if (!(cin >> T)) return 0;\n    while (T--) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 5; ++i) {\n            cout << i << \" - \" << i * i << \"\\n\";\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line = br.readLine();\n        if (line == null || line.isEmpty()) return;\n        int T = Integer.parseInt(line.trim());\n        for (int tc = 0; tc < T; ++tc) {\n            for (int i = 1; i <= 5; ++i) {\n                System.out.println(i + \" - \" + i * i);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    T = int(data[0])\n    out_lines = []\n    for _ in range(T):\n        for i in range(1, 6):\n            out_lines.append(f'{i} - {i * i}')\n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(out_lines) + ('\\n' if out_lines else ''))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()",
      "JavaScript": "const lines = require('fs').readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim().split('\\n');\nlet i = 0;\nconst T = parseInt(lines[i++]);\nlet out = [];\nfor (let tc = 0; tc < T; ++tc) {\n    for (let j = 1; j <= 5; ++j) {\n        out.push(`${j} - ${j * j}`);\n    }\n}\nprocess.stdout.write(out.join('\\n') + (out.length ? '\\n' : ''));"
    },
